{title: The Potter's Hands}
{artist: Darlene Zschech}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Beautiful Lord, [D/F#]wonderful Saviour
[C]I know for sure [Am7]all of my days are [Em7]held in Your hand.
[Asus]Crafted [A]into Your [Am7]perfect [D]plan.

{comment: verse 2}
[G]You gently call me [D/F#]into Your presence
[C]Guiding me by [Am7]Your Holy Spirit, [Em7]teach me dear Lord.
To live [Asus]all of my [A]life  [Am7]through your [D]eyes.

{comment: Pre-Chorus}
[Em]I'm captured by Your holy [D/F#]calling
[G]Set me apart, I [C]know You're [G]drawing [D/F#]me [Em]to Yourself
[A7sus]Lead me [G]Lord, I [Am7]pray.[Dsus]

{comment: Chorus}
[G]Take me, [D/F#]mold me, [Am7]use me, [Bm]fill  [Em7]me,
I [F]give my life [C]to the [Am7]Pot - [Em7]ter's [Am7]hand. [Dsus]    [D]
